# What direction 5 could actually remove — measured 2026-09-08
#
# forge/syncer/tests/push_chain.rs::measure_what_a_refused_push_leaves_in_the_snapshot
# `cargo test --test push_chain measure_what_a_refused_push_leaves_in_the_snapshot -- --nocapture`
#
# Arms N (non-fast-forward), F (refs/for conflict), M (MIXED: one push,
# one ref accepted and one refused), P (policy — the control).
# Corpus: one 4,000-line file, one line edited per push, so pushes DELTIFY.
#
# Direction 5 = name only the packs of pushes something was ACCEPTED from,
# recorded at pre-receive where the quarantine pack is still identifiable.
# Classified here by a recorder wrapped on the real pre-receive hook; a
# push counts as wholly refused iff NONE of the object ids it proposed
# ended up reachable — derived from the final state, not from the
# measurement's own bookkeeping.

## Seven reps

rep  named B   redundant B   %red   d5 removes    d5 keeps (mixed)   d5 keeps (no push)
