  3   157040       145708    92%   116485 (79%)      29223 (20%)          0 (0%)
  4   156768       145472    92%   116486 (80%)      28986 (19%)          0 (0%)
  5   147562       136235    92%   107236 (78%)      28999 (21%)          0 (0%)
  6   166076       154743    93%   125756 (81%)      28987 (18%)          0 (0%)
  7   166053       154728    93%   125743 (81%)      28985 (18%)          0 (0%)

RANGE: direction 5 removes 78-81% of the residue; 18-21% survives it,
all of it in packs from MIXED pushes. Not a mean — the range is the claim.

## Controls

- arm P (refused at pre-receive, before git migrates the quarantine):
  3 quarantine packs built, 0 migrated, 0 named, in every rep.
- THE OTHER ARM: the same predicate on arm N, where git DID migrate —
  3 of 3 present in objects/pack. Without this, `!exists` proves nothing.
- count-objects across arm P is NO LONGER a control in this rig: with arm M
  added the compaction ladder runs continuously, and a base rebuild's output
  (30 objects, 1 pack) lands inside arm P's window in every rep. Shown below
  for the record, not relied on.
- R1 replicated in forge's own chain: 16 of 19 recorded quarantine pack names
  exist in objects/pack afterwards; the 3 that do not are arm P's. If the name
  had not survived `index-pack --fix-thin` + migration, every pack would have
  classified "not from a push" and the answer would have been 0%.
- The recorder's count of wholly-refused pushes (9) is derived from
  reachability and asserted equal to the arms' own count (3+3+3).

## Model runs behind this

ForgeSyncNameAcceptedSet.cfg   HOLDS   25,203,710 distinct, depth 58, 22min 12s
ForgeSyncForgetPushPack.cfg    Inv_LandedPackComplete violated, 1s (the teeth)

